[{"id":"fm-core2-2.21-q1","number":1,"question":"<p>The cross-section of a tunnel is modelled by the curve with equation</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\ny=2p-q\\cosh x\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is the height, in metres, of the tunnel above the road surface, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is the horizontal distance, in metres, from the centre of the tunnel, and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"q\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are positive constants. The tunnel is symmetric about the vertical line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/2.21/questions/assets/diagrams/221q1.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure><p>The tunnel is 6 metres wide at road level and has a maximum height of 6 metres.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find the values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"q\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to three significant figures.</p></li><li><p>A vehicle of rectangular cross-section is to pass through the tunnel. The vehicle is 4 metres wide and 4 metres high. Determine whether the vehicle can pass through the tunnel without touching the sides.</p></li></ol><p><strong>Prerequisite knowledge for Q2: Mean Value and Reversing the Chain Rule</strong></p>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=6\" data-display=\"false\"></span>:</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n6=2p-q\\cosh0\\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad6=2p-q.\\tag{1}\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=3\" data-display=\"false\"></span>:</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n0=2p-q\\cosh3.\\tag{2}\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Solving (1) and (2) gives <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p=3.33084\\ldots=3.33\" data-display=\"false\"></span> (3 SF) and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"q=0.661692\\ldots=0.662\" data-display=\"false\"></span> (3 SF).</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\ny =2(3.33084\\ldots)-0.661692\\ldots\\cosh x,\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\ny\\big|_{x=2} =6.6616\\ldots-0.661692\\ldots\\cosh2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =4.1722\\ldots.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>The vehicle is 4 metres tall and the tunnel is at least 4.17 metres tall (3 SF) if the vehicle drives so that its centre is also at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. So yes, the vehicle can pass through the tunnel without touching the sides.</p>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.21-q2","number":2,"question":"<p>The temperature, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T^\\circ\\mathrm{C}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, of a chemical solution <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\" data-display=\"false\"></span> hours after a catalyst is added can be modelled by the equation</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nT=60-15\\tanh0.8t\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\\geq0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Using the model, determine the mean temperature of the solution during the first 45 minutes of the catalyst being added, giving your answer correct to two decimal places.</p>","steps":["<p>The mean temperature during the first 45 minutes is</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\frac1{0.75-0}\\int_0^{0.75}(60-15\\tanh0.8t)\\,dt\n =\\frac43\\left[60t-\\frac{75}{4}\\ln|\\cosh0.8t|\\right]_0^{0.75}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =\\frac43\\left(45-\\frac{75}{4}\\ln\\left|\\cosh\\frac35\\right|-(0-0)\\right)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =60-25\\ln\\left|\\cosh\\frac35\\right|\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =55.7466\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =55.75^\\circ\\mathrm C\\quad(2\\ \\mathrm{DP}).\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.21-q3","number":3,"question":"<p>The velocity, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"v\\,\\mathrm{m\\,s^{-1}}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, of a skydiver <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\" data-display=\"false\"></span> seconds after leaving a stationary helicopter is modelled by</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nv=55\\tanh(0.12t)\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\\geq0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Explain why this model predicts the existence of a terminal velocity, and state its value.</p></li><li><p>According to the model, find the time taken for the skydiver to reach 90% of the terminal velocity. Give your answer to 2 decimal places.</p></li></ol><p><strong>Prerequisite knowledge for Q4: Volume of Revolution and Hyperbolic Identities</strong></p>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>As <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\\to\\infty\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\tanh(0.12t)\\to1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"v\\to55\\times1=55\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. The model suggests that the terminal velocity is 55 <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm{m\\,s^{-1}}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>90% of the terminal velocity is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0.9\\times55=49.5\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n55\\tanh(0.12t) =49.5\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\Rightarrow\\tanh(0.12t) =0.9\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\Rightarrow0.12t =\\operatorname{artanh}0.9\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\Rightarrow t =\\frac{25}{3}\\times\\frac12\\ln\\left(\\frac{1+0.9}{1-0.9}\\right)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =\\frac{25}{6}\\ln19\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =12.268\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =12.27\\text{ seconds (2 DP).}\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.21-q4","number":4,"question":"<p>A water treatment company is designing a large filtration pipe. The inside wall of the pipe is modelled by the curve</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\ny=2+\\cosh\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-4\\leq x\\leq4\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are measured in metres. The pipe is formed by rotating the region enclosed by the curve and the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-axis about the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-axis.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Show that the volume <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"V\" data-display=\"false\"></span> of the pipe is 381 <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm{m^3}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to the nearest cubic metre.</p></li><li><p>The pipe can process 0.85 <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm{m^3}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> of water per second when completely full. Estimate how many seconds are needed to completely fill the pipe.</p></li></ol><p><strong>Prerequisite knowledge for Q5: Differentiation of Hyperbolic Functions</strong></p>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nV =\\pi\\int_{-4}^{4}\\left(2+\\cosh\\frac{x}{2}\\right)^2dx\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =\\pi\\int_{-4}^{4}\\left(4+4\\cosh\\frac{x}{2}+\\cosh^2\\frac{x}{2}\\right)dx.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Since <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\cosh^2A=\\frac12\\cosh2A+\\frac12\" data-display=\"false\"></span>,</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nV =\\pi\\int_{-4}^{4}\\left(4+4\\cosh\\frac{x}{2}+\\frac12\\cosh x+\\frac12\\right)dx\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =\\pi\\int_{-4}^{4}\\left(\\frac92+4\\cosh\\frac{x}{2}+\\frac12\\cosh x\\right)dx\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =\\pi\\left[\\frac92x+8\\sinh\\frac{x}{2}+\\frac12\\sinh x\\right]_{-4}^{4}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =\\pi\\left[\\left(18+8\\sinh2+\\frac12\\sinh4\\right)-\\left(-18+8\\sinh(-2)+\\frac12\\sinh(-4)\\right)\\right]\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =381.1370271\\ldots.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Therefore <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"V=381\\,\\mathrm{m^3}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to the nearest cubic metre.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>The pipe fills at a rate of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0.85\\,\\mathrm{m^3s^{-1}}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, so</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\frac{381}{0.85}=448.235\\ldots.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>It takes approximately 448 seconds.</p>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.21-q5","number":5,"question":"<p>Light travelling through water decreases in intensity with depth. In a particular model, the intensity <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"I\" data-display=\"false\"></span> at a depth of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> metres below the surface is given by</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nI=I_0\\sech(kx)\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"I_0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is the intensity at the surface, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a positive constant, and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\\geq0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/2.21/questions/assets/diagrams/221q5.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Show that the depth <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> at which the intensity is equal to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"fI_0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0&lt;f&lt;1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, is given by <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle x=\\frac1k\\operatorname{arcosh}\\left(\\frac1f\\right)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li><li><p>Given that the intensity is reduced to 40% of its surface value at a depth of 12 metres, find the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, giving your answer to 3 significant figures.</p></li><li><p>Given that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"I_0=120\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, find an expression for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\frac{dI}{dx}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> in terms of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li><li><p>Using your value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\" data-display=\"false\"></span> from part (b), find the rate of change of light intensity with respect to depth when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=8\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, giving your answer to 3 significant figures.</p></li><li><p>Show that the magnitude of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\frac{dI}{dx}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> decreases as <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> increases for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\\geq0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Hence explain what this suggests about the behaviour of light as it enters the water.</p></li><li><p>Given that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sech u\\approx1-\\frac{u^2}{2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> for small values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"u\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, comment on how well the model represents light intensity close to the surface.</p></li></ol><p><strong>Prerequisite knowledge for Q6: Harmonic Form, Hyperbolic Identities and Second Order Homogeneous Differential Equations</strong></p>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"I=fI_0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>:</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nfI_0 =I_0\\sech(kx)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\Rightarrow f =\\sech(kx)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\Rightarrow\\frac1f =\\cosh(kx)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\Rightarrow kx =\\operatorname{arcosh}\\left(\\frac1f\\right)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\Rightarrow x =\\frac1k\\operatorname{arcosh}\\left(\\frac1f\\right).\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f=0.4\" data-display=\"false\"></span> when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=12\" data-display=\"false\"></span>:</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n12 =\\frac1k\\operatorname{arcosh}\\left(\\frac1{0.4}\\right)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\Rightarrow k =\\frac1{12}\\operatorname{arcosh}\\frac52\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =\\frac1{12}\\ln\\left(\\frac52+\\sqrt{\\left(\\frac52\\right)^2-1}\\right)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =\\frac1{12}\\ln\\left(\\frac52+\\frac{\\sqrt{21}}2\\right)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =0.1305666\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\therefore k =0.131\\quad(3\\ \\mathrm{SF}).\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nI_0=120,\\qquad I=120\\sech(kx),\\qquad \\frac{dI}{dx}=-120k\\tanh(kx)\\sech(kx).\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\left.\\frac{dI}{dx}\\right|_{x=8} =-120\\times0.131\\tanh(8\\times0.131)\\sech(8\\times0.131)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =-7.66741\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =-7.67\\quad(3\\ \\mathrm{SF}).\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">e)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\frac{dI}{dx} =-120\\times0.131\\tanh(0.131x)\\sech(0.131x)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =-15.72\\tanh(0.131x)\\sech(0.131x).\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>For <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\\geq0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, we have <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\tanh(0.131x)\\geq0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sech(0.131x)&gt;0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{dI}{dx}\\leq0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. As <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> increases, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sech(0.131x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> decreases, and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\tanh(0.131x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> increases but is bounded from above by 1. So <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\tanh(0.131x)\\sech(0.131x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> decreases for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\\geq0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Therefore <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\left|\\frac{dI}{dx}\\right|\" data-display=\"false\"></span> decreases as <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> increases for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\\geq0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. This suggests that the light intensity decreases most rapidly near the surface of the water, and that the rate at which intensity decreases becomes smaller with increasing depth.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">f)</h3><p>For small <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"u\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sech u\\approx1-\\frac{u^2}{2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. So</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\sech(kx)\\approx1-\\frac{(kx)^2}{2}=1-\\frac{k^2x^2}{2}\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>for small values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Therefore</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nI=120\\sech(kx)\\approx120\\left(1-\\frac{k^2x^2}{2}\\right)=120-60k^2x^2.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>This approximation suggests that, close to the surface, the intensity of light decreases approximately quadratically with depth. This supports the model's prediction of a rapid initial decrease in intensity as the light enters the water.</p>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.21-q6","number":6,"question":"<ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"e^{kt}\\equiv\\cosh kt+\\sinh kt\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li></ol><p>The displacement, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> metres, of a particle at time <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\" data-display=\"false\"></span> seconds is governed by the differential equation</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\frac{d^2x}{dt^2}-9x=0.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>Initially, the particle is at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and is moving with velocity 3 <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm{m\\,s^{-1}}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>[b)] Show that the general solution can be written in the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=A\\cosh3t+B\\sinh3t\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are constants to be found.</p></li><li><p>[c)] Express the solution in the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=R\\cosh(3t+\\alpha)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li><li><p>[d)] Find the time at which the displacement of the particle is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2\\sqrt3\" data-display=\"false\"></span> metres, giving your answer in the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\frac16\\ln(a+b\\sqrt3)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are rational numbers.</p></li></ol><p><strong>Prerequisite knowledge for Q7: Differentiation and Integration of Hyperbolic Functions</strong></p>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\text{RHS:}\\quad\\cosh kt+\\sinh kt\n \\equiv\\frac{e^{kt}+e^{-kt}}2+\\frac{e^{kt}-e^{-kt}}2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n \\equiv\\frac12(e^{kt}+e^{kt})+\\frac12(e^{-kt}-e^{-kt})\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n \\equiv e^{kt}\\quad\\text{: LHS, as required.}\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\frac{d^2x}{dt^2}-9x =0,\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\text{AE:}\\quad m^2-9 =0\\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad m=3\\text{ or }m=-3,\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\therefore x =Pe^{3t}+Qe^{-3t}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =P(\\cosh3t+\\sinh3t)+Q(\\cosh(-3t)+\\sinh(-3t))\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =P(\\cosh3t+\\sinh3t)+Q(\\cosh3t-\\sinh3t)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =(P+Q)\\cosh3t+(P-Q)\\sinh3t\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =A\\cosh3t+B\\sinh3t,\\quad\\text{where }A=P+Q,\\ B=P-Q.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>:</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n2=A\\cosh0+B\\sinh0\\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad A=2.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>So <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=2\\cosh3t+B\\sinh3t\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nv=\\frac{dx}{dt}=6\\sinh3t+3B\\cosh3t.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"v=3\" data-display=\"false\"></span>:</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n3=6\\sinh0+3B\\cosh0\\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad3=3B\\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad B=1.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Therefore <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=2\\cosh3t+\\sinh3t\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nR\\cosh(3t+\\alpha) \\equiv R(\\cosh3t\\cosh\\alpha+\\sinh3t\\sinh\\alpha)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n \\equiv R\\cosh\\alpha\\cosh3t+R\\sinh\\alpha\\sinh3t.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Thus <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R\\cosh\\alpha=2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R=\\frac2{\\cosh\\alpha}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>; and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R\\sinh\\alpha=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R=\\frac1{\\sinh\\alpha}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Hence</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\frac2{\\cosh\\alpha} =\\frac1{\\sinh\\alpha}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\Rightarrow\\frac{\\sinh\\alpha}{\\cosh\\alpha} =\\frac12\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\Rightarrow\\tanh\\alpha =\\frac12\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\Rightarrow\\alpha =\\operatorname{artanh}\\frac12\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =\\frac12\\ln\\left(\\frac{1+1/2}{1-1/2}\\right)=\\frac12\\ln3.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nR =\\frac2{\\cosh(\\frac12\\ln3)}=\\frac2{\\frac{e^{\\frac12\\ln3}+e^{-\\frac12\\ln3}}2}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =\\frac4{\\sqrt3+1/\\sqrt3}=\\frac{4\\sqrt3}{3+1}=\\sqrt3.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Therefore <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=\\sqrt3\\cosh\\left(3t+\\frac12\\ln3\\right)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n2\\sqrt3 =\\sqrt3\\cosh\\left(3t+\\frac12\\ln3\\right)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\Rightarrow\\cosh\\left(3t+\\frac12\\ln3\\right) =2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\Rightarrow3t+\\frac12\\ln3 =\\operatorname{arcosh}2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\Rightarrow t =\\frac13\\operatorname{arcosh}2-\\frac16\\ln3\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =\\frac13\\ln(2+\\sqrt{2^2-1})-\\frac16\\ln3\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =\\frac13\\ln(2+\\sqrt3)-\\frac16\\ln3\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =\\frac16\\left(2\\ln(2+\\sqrt3)-\\ln3\\right)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =\\frac16\\left(\\ln(2+\\sqrt3)^2-\\ln3\\right)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =\\frac16\\left(\\ln(7+4\\sqrt3)-\\ln3\\right)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =\\frac16\\ln\\left(\\frac73+\\frac43\\sqrt3\\right).\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.21-q7","number":7,"question":"<p>A small research rocket is launched vertically upwards. Its velocity, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"v\\,\\mathrm{m\\,s^{-1}}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, at time <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\" data-display=\"false\"></span> seconds after launch is modelled by the equation</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nv=A\\sinh kt\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are positive constants.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Show that the acceleration of the rocket, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\\,\\mathrm{m\\,s^{-2}}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, can be expressed in the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a=k\\sqrt{v^2+A^2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li><li><p>It is given that the initial acceleration of the rocket is 2 <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm{m\\,s^{-2}}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. It is also known that when the rocket reaches a velocity of 12 <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm{m\\,s^{-1}}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, its acceleration is 5.2 <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm{m\\,s^{-2}}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Find the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li><li><p>Show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k=0.4\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li><li><p>Find the distance travelled by the rocket in the first 5 seconds of its launch, giving your answer to the nearest metre.</p></li></ol><p><strong>Prerequisite knowledge for Q8: Integration using Inverse Hyperbolic Functions</strong></p>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\na =\\frac{dv}{dt}=Ak\\cosh kt\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =Ak\\sqrt{\\cosh^2kt}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =Ak\\sqrt{1+\\sinh^2kt}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =k\\sqrt{A^2(1+\\sinh^2kt)}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =k\\sqrt{A^2+A^2\\sinh^2kt}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =k\\sqrt{(A\\sinh kt)^2+A^2}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =k\\sqrt{v^2+A^2}.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a=2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>:</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n2=Ak\\cosh0\\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad Ak=2\\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad k=\\frac2A.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"v=12\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a=5.2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>:</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n5.2 =k\\sqrt{12^2+A^2}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\Rightarrow5.2 =\\frac2A\\sqrt{144+A^2}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\Rightarrow2.6A =\\sqrt{144+A^2}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\Rightarrow6.76A^2 =144+A^2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\Rightarrow5.76A^2 =144\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\Rightarrow A^2 =25\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\Rightarrow A =5.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nk=\\frac25=0.4.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\int_0^5 5\\sinh(0.4t)\\,dt\n =\\left[\\frac{25}{2}\\cosh(0.4t)\\right]_0^5\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =\\frac{25}{2}\\cosh2-\\frac{25}{2}\\cosh0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =34.52744\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =35\\text{ metres to the nearest metre.}\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.21-q8","number":8,"question":"<p>A farmer is designing a new barn for storing hay. The cross-section of the barn is modelled for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-6\\leq x\\leq6\" data-display=\"false\"></span> by the curve</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\ny=\\frac{12}{\\sqrt{x^2+9}}.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/2.21/questions/assets/diagrams/221q8.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure><p>The region enclosed by the curve, the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-axis, and the lines <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=-6\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=6\" data-display=\"false\"></span> represents the cross-sectional area of the barn. Each unit on the axes represents 2 metres. The barn is modelled as a prism of length 18 metres.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Show that the cross-sectional area of the barn is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"96\\ln(2+\\sqrt5)\\,\\mathrm{m^2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li><li><p>Find the volume of the barn, giving your answer to the nearest <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm{m^3}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li><li><p>The farmer stores hay bales occupying 1.8 <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm{m^3}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Estimate the maximum number of hay bales that can fit inside the barn.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nA =\\int_{-6}^{6}\\frac{12}{\\sqrt{x^2+9}}\\,dx\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =\\int_{-6}^{6}\\frac{12}{\\sqrt{9(\\frac19x^2+1)}}\\,dx\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =\\int_{-6}^{6}\\frac{12}{3\\sqrt{(\\frac13x)^2+1}}\\,dx\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =4\\int_{-6}^{6}\\frac1{\\sqrt{(\\frac13x)^2+1}}\\,dx\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =4\\left[3\\operatorname{arsinh}\\left(\\frac{x}{3}\\right)\\right]_{-6}^{6}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =12\\ln(2+\\sqrt{2^2+1})-12\\ln(-2+\\sqrt{(-2)^2+1})\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =12\\ln(2+\\sqrt5)-12\\ln(-2+\\sqrt5)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =12\\ln\\left(\\frac{2+\\sqrt5}{-2+\\sqrt5}\\right)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =12\\ln(9+4\\sqrt5).\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Since <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"9+4\\sqrt5=(2+\\sqrt5)^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, then</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nA=12\\ln((2+\\sqrt5)^2)=24\\ln(2+\\sqrt5).\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Each unit represents 2 m, so the area scale factor is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2^2=4\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Therefore the actual area is</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n4\\times24\\ln(2+\\sqrt5)=96\\ln(2+\\sqrt5)\\,\\mathrm{m^2},\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>as required.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nV =\\text{cross-sectional area}\\times\\text{length}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =96\\ln(2+\\sqrt5)\\times18\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =1728\\ln(2+\\sqrt5)\\,\\mathrm{m^3}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =2495\\,\\mathrm{m^3}.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p>Each hay bale occupies <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"1.8\\,\\mathrm{m^3}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, so the number of bales is</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\frac{2495}{1.8}=1386.111\\ldots.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>So 1386 hay bales.</p>"]}]